the MIT License (see LICENSE).

Vendored commit: 4c504c93 (tag: 2.13.1)

Vendored directories/files (under `src/vendor/`):

  - extraction/**            (hard-string extraction: rules, babel/html parsers)
  - parsers/**               (locale file format parsers: json, json5, yaml, ini,
                               po, php, properties, ftl, ecmascript)
  - frameworks/**             (all i18n framework definitions: vue, react-i18next,
                               i18next, ngx-translate, flutter, rails, laravel, etc.)
  - packagesParsers/**        (package.json / pubspec.yaml / composer.json / Gemfile
                               parsers used to detect framework config)
  - core/KeyDetector.ts, core/Analyst.ts, core/types.ts
  - core/Nodes.ts, core/Errors.ts, core/Telemetry.ts, core/Translator.ts
                               (pulled in transitively by core/loaders/**)
  - core/loaders/**           (ComposedLoader, LocaleLoader, VueSfcLoader,
                               FluentVueSfcLoader, Loader base class)
  - meta.ts                   (shared constants, pulled in by Nodes.ts/LocaleLoader.ts)
  - utils/glob.ts and small utils it/the above files depend on (Log, LanguageId,
    utils, UnicodeDecorator, UnicodeProgressBar, NodeHelper, File, Regex, flat,
    flags, cache, PathMatcher, prompts, shared, keypathValidate, index)

Every vendored file carries a header comment:

  // Vendored from lokalise/i18n-ally @4c504c93 — MIT. See NOTICE.

IMPORTANT — these files were copied verbatim (not adapted) and will NOT compile
as-is. They still contain unresolved imports of:

  - `vscode` (the VS Code extension API — not available outside the editor)
  - `./Global` / `../Global` / `~/core` (core/Global.ts, the extension's global
    singleton)
  - `./Config` / `../Config` / `~/core` (core/Config.ts, the extension's
    workspace-config singleton)
  - `./CurrentFile` / `~/core` (core/CurrentFile.ts — holds VS Code editor/
    document state; equally extension-runtime-coupled and was NOT vendored)
  - a handful of other extension-only modules reached transitively through
    core/loaders/** and core/Telemetry.ts / core/Translator.ts: `~/i18n`,
    `~/env`, `~/extension`, `~/views`, `~/commands` (incl.
    `~/commands/manipulations`), `~/translators`, `@amplitude/analytics-node`

These are intentionally left untouched; replacing them with CLI-appropriate
shims is the responsibility of the next lane. See the Fixer report for the
full file:line inventory.

